    "note": "**MASTER CANDIDATE — the ship gate for `@m0saic/dsl-tutorial/v1`.**\n\nA clean app-shell showcase — passthrough **hero** (`4(0,0,0,F)` → full-width) · **sidebar + 3-row content** (`2(F,3[F,F,F])`) · footer — in the new **light** default. It exercises passthrough donation, nested splits, the inspector fields, and the camera in one legible walk.\n\n**What's validated (the whole pre-master suite, all approved):**\n\n| dimension | candidate |\n|---|---|\n| camera zoom + end-hold | 01-b |\n| DSL paging | 02 |\n| passthrough (single + multi) | 03, 09 |\n| null slots | 04 |\n| overlays (single + complex multi) | 05-a, 10 |\n| F frames + portrait canvas | 06 |\n| square output + light + panel toggles | 07-b |\n| chromeless reflow | 08-a |\n\nPlus the W1 perf win (canvas 228s → ~5s at 10×10), rounded corners preserved, N=3 split-count fix, panel-hide reflow, and the header divider.\n\n**This is a TEMPLATE approval, not a frame.** Try to break it — I'd hit: extreme grids (16×16), a >2000-char DSL, `preset: dark` (the IDE look), all panels hidden but one, non-default aspect (portrait/square output), `speedMultiplier` at 0.25 and 8, a single `F`, and a null-heavy layout. I pre-verified this showcase renders clean at **landscape, portrait, and square** output.\n\n**Say \"ship it\"** and I promote this to `master.mosaicx` + `master.mosaic`, wire the preview asset, write `postmortem.mosaicx`, and prep the lock (unit + CLI-E2E case + `e2eTemplateVariants` entry). Prefer **dark** for the shipped showcase, or a different layout? Tell me before I promote.",
